###########
# NOTES
###########
# The option --rfdist compute the topological Robinson-Foulds (RF) distance among all resulting trees. It's possible to use this metrics as a measure of
# topological uncertainty by examining the .rfDistances file.
# Output file contains 4 columns: 1st and 2nd column contain tree indices in the NEWICK file, 3rd column shows the absolute RF distance between those two trees,
# and 4th column shows the relative or normalized RF distance ranging from 0 to 1. Relative RF distance is calculated by dividing the absolute value (column 3)
# by the maximum possible RF distance for this tree pair

